  "steps": [
    {
      "kind": "see",
      "title": "See it",
      "text": "The fers-alfil moves like a fers or an alfil: one square diagonally, or a jump of exactly two squares diagonally over whatever stands in between. It takes the same way. Shako, a chess variant on a 10 by 10 board, calls this piece the elephant. The marked squares are every square it can reach.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "e": "fersAlfil" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3E4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4"
    },
    {
      "kind": "try",
      "title": "Try it",
      "text": "Move the fers-alfil to each marked square, one after the other.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "e": "fersAlfil" }, "fen": "k7/8/8/8/3E4/8/8/7K w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4",
      "targets": ["f6", "g5"]
    },
    {
      "kind": "read",
      "title": "Strategy",
      "pages": [
        {
          "text": "The fers-alfil is worth a little less than a knight or a bishop. It reaches eight squares from the middle of the board, but like a bishop it stays on squares of one colour all game: this one can never reach a light square.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "e": "fersAlfil" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3E4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "e5"], ["d4", "f6"]]
        },
        {
          "text": "Because it jumps, the fers-alfil can come out from behind a wall of pawns. It guards the squares diagonally next to it and two squares away, so it is a good partner for a knight or a rook, which can reach the squares it can't. Here it guards the knight on b2.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "e": "fersAlfil" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3E4/8/1N6/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } }
        },
        {
          "text": "It can't move straight. Here the black rook attacks it from d5, and the fers-alfil can't take it back, so it jumps away.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "e": "fersAlfil" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/3r4/3E4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "f6"]]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "puzzles",
      "title": "Puzzles",
      "puzzles": [
        {
          "prompt": "Take a black pawn.",
